                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238091558",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198931247655",
                            "num_reviews": 22,
                            "playtime_forever": 839,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 839,
                            "last_played": 1792415476
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A pretty good retro RPG with some ADV/VN tendencies and a cool narrative gimmick; basically, most of the game is a series of flashbacks that take place during the five minutes in which the amnesiac hero is fighting the Demon King and trying to remember how he even got there. The world is fun to explore and there's some charm to the game overall. You might find yourself using your Repel spell a lot later on to stop random encounters, however, as the rate is too high and later dungeons are too large. It doesn't help that enemies and bosses are all far too easy, so there's no real interest in fighting them. At least battles are quick. IMO it's better than many other retro RPGs I've played that found more success.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1792415962,
